2026-07-27 22:06:59,351 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3d3f389a-3fd2-464b-86ed-e77d9316f532', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7fe7c77f3ec0>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': 'Microsoft SharePoint under attack via new exploit\n\nMicrosoft released security updates to address CVE-2026-50522 and said customers should upgrade to the latest version, a spokesperson told Cybersecurity Dive. The company is not aware of any exploitation prior to publishing the CVE. “The security update fully mitigates the issue, however rotating machine keys can be performed to further safeguard user environments,” the spokesperson said. The Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency on Wednesday added CVE-2026-50522 to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog. CISA set a deadline of Friday for Federal Civilian Executive Branch agencies to take steps to mitigate the flaw. CISA cannot confirm whether the vulnerability has been used in ransomware activity, according to the listing. CISA alert\nJust one week ago, CISA warned of three vulnerabilities in SharePoint facing exploitation:\xa0\n\nAn improper input validation vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-32201, allows an attacker to perform spoofing over a network. A remote code execution vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-45659, involves deserialization of untrusted data.', 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
