2026-07-27 22:07:47,175 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e876d70d-591f-41c3-9c1c-965576e153b8', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7fe7c75868e0>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': "NVIDIA Forms 37-Member Open Secure AI Alliance and Open-Sources NOOA Framework\n\nThe alliance follows a July 24 industry letter arguing that downloadable models give defenders capabilities comparable to attackers, reduce dependence on individual providers, and allow sensitive work to remain on infrastructure controlled by the user. OpenAI, Google, and Meta appear among the letter's signatories but are absent from the alliance's inaugural membership list. Anthropic appears on neither list as of July 27, 2026. The roster alone does not explain those absences. Signing the policy letter and joining a technical coalition are different commitments, and the public materials do not say why those companies are absent, whether membership discussions are underway, or what members must contribute to join. Several technologies cited in the announcement predate the coalition, including Hugging Face's Safetensors model format, HPE-backed SPIFFE/SPIRE workload identity, IBM and Red Hat's Lightwell remediation system, Microsoft's MDASH multi-model security harness, and SpaceXAI's Grok Build coding agent. They are member projects, not alliance-created products.", 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
