2026-07-29 21:52:44,877 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-5c4a5534-766c-4a9d-a24c-2622e163e548', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7f6a0b7feb60>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': '24,650 Internet-Exposed BMCs Disclose IPMI Password Hashes Before Login\n\nIt\'s not clear who is behind the activity. That said, HPE iLO servers have been singled out as far back as 2020 to deploy a rootkit called iLOBleed. To counter the risk, it\'s advised to block UDP port 623 at the network edge, rotate factory-issued passwords during provisioning, disable legacy or weak options such as IPMI 1.5, restrict BMC access to a dedicated private management network, and apply network access controls to ensure only approved administrative systems can reach BMC interfaces. "Organizations have spent years hardening cloud workloads and operating systems, but many have overlooked the infrastructure that sits beneath them," said Yakir Kadkoda, CTO and co-founder at Lava, in a statement.', 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
