2026-07-29 23:06:55,845 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-b932596b-6393-4483-8136-064b12bae10f', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7f7c7818a660>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': "ENISA on Air: Our first podcast launches on Frontier AI\n\nENISA launches a podcast series to decrypt the latest cybersecurity developments and discuss issues that shape Europe's cybersecurity landscape. ENISA wanted to provide its audiences with a new channel to share updates from the Agency but importantly to create a space where we will have the opportunity to promote ENISA’s cybersecurity expertise and raise awareness for EU level cybersecurity and its opportunities. Through this podcast series, the Agency looks at the risks, the trends, the decisions that matter from cyber resilience to emerging technologies to trust and cooperation needed for Europe's digital future. Hosted by ENISA Associate Chief Cybersecurity and Operations Officer Florian Pennings and ENISA Spokesperson Laura Heuvinck, this first series will bring a number of podcasts throughout 2026. For our first episode, we welcomed Jaya Baloo, co-founder of AISLE™ and Razvan Gavrila, Head of Sector at ENISA, to explore the latest developments and impact of Frontier AI on cybersecurity. In July 2026, the Agency published a note on ‘ENISA’s View on Cybersecurity in the Frontier AI Era’\xa0which provides national competent authorities in Member States and EU policymakers, defenders, and service providers with an initial set of recommendations to support them in their respective roles towards developing the necessary operational capabilities to face machine-speed threats. Future episodes will address on key cybersecurity topics such as Europe’s cyber threat landscape, vulnerability management as well as flagship ENISA work such as the upcoming Single Reporting Platform and State of Cybersecurity in the Union 2026 report. Tune in, follow along and join the conversation!", 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
