2026-07-29 23:07:17,650 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-85c533f6-4337-4121-af60-84c1c233e4cd', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7f7c756d99e0>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': 'Ruflo MCP Flaw Lets Unauthenticated Attackers Run Commands and Poison AI Memory\n\nThe crux of the vulnerability is that Ruflo exposed 233 tools, including shell command execution, database operations, agent management, and memory storage, through an unauthenticated Model Context Protocol (MCP) bridge that\'s open to the network by default. Specifically, the "docker-compose.yml" YAML configuration file was found to bind port 3001 to 0.0.0.0 by default, exposing the bridge on all network interfaces. That said, the extent of exposure depends on the deployment\'s firewall rules, security groups, and network segmentation.', 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
