2026-08-02 17:14:36,528 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f14edc1d-13e7-40ab-a965-992696d399a4', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7f14254a2c00>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': 'Cisco FMC Zero-Day Actively Exploited, Static Credentials Could Expose Sensitive Data\n\nCisco also acknowledged that it became actively exploited earlier this month, although it did not disclose when the attacks began, who is behind them, or how the vulnerability is being exploited in these efforts. The issue has been addressed in the following hot fix versions of Cisco Secure FMC Software -\n\n7.0 - Cisco_Firepower_Mgmt_Center_Hotfix_GB-7.0.9.1-3.sh.REL.tar\n7.2 - Cisco_Secure_FW_Mgmt_Center_Hotfix_HL-7.2.11.1-4.sh.REL.tar\n7.4 - Cisco_Secure_FW_Mgmt_Center_Hotfix_HG-7.4.7.1-3.sh.REL.tar\n7.6 - Cisco_Secure_FW_Mgmt_Center_Hotfix_CY-7.6.5.1-2.sh.REL.tar\n7.7 - Cisco_Secure_FW_Mgmt_Center_Hotfix_AM-7.7.12.1-2.sh.REL.tar\n10.0 - Cisco_Secure_FW_Mgmt_Center_Hotfix_P-10.0.1.1-2.sh.REL.tar\n\nAs indicators of compromise (IoCs), Cisco is urging customers to use the "cat /var/log/messages | grep license" CLI command in expert mode. If the command output includes "/var/tmp/license.tmp," there is a possibility that the vulnerability may have been exploited on the Cisco Secure FMC device -\nroot@firepower:/home/admin# cat /var/log/messages | grep license\nJul 23 16:16:33 firepower sudo:      www : PWD=/ ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/local/sf/bin/package_info.pl /var/tmp/license.tmp --lsm\n\nIn tandem, Cisco has updated its advisory for CVE-2026-20079 (CVSS score: 10.0), a critical authentication bypass flaw impacting Cisco Secure FMC Software, to include a second bug ID ("CSCwt95974"), the same indicators of compromise, and hot fixes. However, the company said it is not aware of malicious exploitation of this vulnerability.', 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
