2026-08-04 06:00:56,018 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8c95e3bb-4cf2-4c73-9bf3-1b0c9c01b7fb', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7fde36904540>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': '18 Malicious npm Packages Deliver Cross-Platform RAT to Alibaba Tool Users\n\nCybersecurity researchers have discovered a new set of malicious npm packages that target users of Alibaba developer tools with a cross-platform remote access trojan (RAT) as part of a sophisticated, targeted software supply chain attack targeting Chinese-speaking environments. One of the packages in question is "lib-mtop," an unscoped package with the same name as a private Alibaba package under the "@ali" scope. Although the npm package was first published sometime in November 2023 with no functionality, three new versions (v1.0.1, v1.0.2, and v1.0.3) were uploaded earlier this March and April.', 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
