2026-08-04 06:13:17,106 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-271ed439-3f3a-4e40-80b0-ed0a3d542796', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7f9246ce6a20>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': '18 Malicious npm Packages Deliver Cross-Platform RAT to Alibaba Tool Users\n\nCybersecurity researchers have discovered a new set of malicious npm packages that target users of Alibaba developer tools with a cross-platform remote access trojan (RAT) as part of a sophisticated, targeted software supply chain attack targeting Chinese-speaking environments. One of the packages in question is "lib-mtop," an unscoped package with the same name as a private Alibaba package under the "@ali" scope. Although the npm package was first published sometime in November 2023 with no functionality, three new versions (v1.0.1, v1.0.2, and v1.0.3) were uploaded earlier this March and April.', 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
