2026-08-04 06:13:25,069 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-ac5eae72-8774-490d-a206-f4cd0cddedb9', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7f9246ce6a20>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': "FOMO in the SOC: Where AI Platforms like Claude Actually Fit\n\nAI is moving incredibly fast, and every security leader is feeling the pressure to keep up. AI platforms like Claude, Codex and Cursor are already helping security teams write detections, investigate alerts, summarize incidents, and automate repetitive work. The conversation has evolved from whether AI belongs in the SOC, to where each type of AI delivers the most value. With so many new AI products entering the market, it's easy to assume one tool can solve every problem. In reality, different types of AI are designed for different jobs. Understanding that difference is what transforms AI FOMO into better security outcomes. Join AI SOC: Where Claude belongs in the SOC\nAI is changing security operations\nThe way security teams work is changing quickly. Attackers are already using AI to generate phishing campaigns, automate malware development, and move faster than ever before.", 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
