2026-08-04 06:13:25,850 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3f76dba5-f060-42c4-81cd-d022c5c1875e', 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x7f9246ce6a20>, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'input': "FOMO in the SOC: Where AI Platforms like Claude Actually Fit\n\nDraft and refine detection rules. Hunt for emerging threats. Summarize investigations for stakeholders. Generate incident reports. Explore new hypotheses. Make the final decisions on complex cases. In other words, the autonomous AI SOC handles the grind of triaging endless alerts and repetitive investigation. The AI platform helps people think, create, and decide based on everything the AI SOC has provided. Better together\nThe biggest takeaway isn't that organizations need to choose between an autonomous AI SOC and AI platforms like Claude. They need both.", 'model': 'text-embedding-3-small', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
